      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Area of sector $CPQ$ is $\\frac12(4^2)(\\pi/3)=\\frac{8\\pi}{3}$ — M1. Area of the segment beyond $CPQ$ is $\\frac{8\\pi}{3}-\\frac12(4^2)\\sin(\\pi/3)=\\frac{8\\pi}{3}-4\\sqrt3$ — M1. Area of one small semicircle is $\\frac12\\pi(2^2)$ (or the small-circle area is $\\pi2^2$) — M1. Obtain the plate area by subtracting the two small semicircles and two segments from the large circle — M1. $16\\pi-4\\pi-2(\\frac{8\\pi}{3}-4\\sqrt3)=\\frac{20\\pi}{3}+8\\sqrt3$ — A1, AG. Alternative: use two sectors $PCS$, two triangles $PCQ$, and two small semicircles; corresponding formulae and final result receive M1 M1 M1 M1 A1. Total: 5.",
